#. fr: nautiles sombres
#. column 0: dark nautilus
#. column 8: Known for its ability to survive on aether alone, researchers are willing to part with huge sums of gil for live samples.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
#. column 9: Dark Nautilus
msgctxt "Item:29742:0:2"
msgid "dark nautiluses"
msgstr "тёмные наутилусы"

#. ja: ロータノ海に棲息する有殻の頭足類<br>[魚拓額縁G2に設定可能]
#. de: Dieser Kopffüßer lebt in den Tiefen der Rhotano-See. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe M ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Une espèce de céphalopode endémique à la mer de Rhotano.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de taille moyenne]
#. column 0: dark nautilus
#. column 2: dark nautiluses
#. column 9: Dark Nautilus
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:29742:0:8"
msgid "Known for its ability to survive on aether alone, researchers are willing to part with huge sums of gil for live samples.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]"
msgstr "Этот головоногий моллюск умеет обходиться одним эфиром. Исследователи готовы выложить за живой экземпляр целое состояние в гилах.<br><br>[Можно выставить в рамке для среднего ихтиопринта.]"

#. ja: ダークノーチラス
#. de: Finster-Perlboot
#. fr: Nautile sombre
#. column 0: dark nautilus
#. column 2: dark nautiluses
#. column 8: Known for its ability to survive on aether alone, researchers are willing to part with huge sums of gil for live samples.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:29742:0:9"
msgid "Dark Nautilus"
msgstr "Тёмный наутилус"

#. ja: エルダー・ディニクティス
#. de: Tiefsee-Dunkleosteus
#. fr: dinichthys ancien
#. column 2: elder dinichthys
#. column 8: Swims about the Strait of Merlthor as though it owns the place─a claim which few of the other inhabitants are in any position to dispute.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Elder Dinichthys
msgctxt "Item:29743:0:0"
msgid "elder dinichthys"
msgstr "старый динихтис"

#. de: Tiefsee-Dunkleosteusse
#. fr: dinichthys anciens
#. column 0: elder dinichthys
#. column 8: Swims about the Strait of Merlthor as though it owns the place─a claim which few of the other inhabitants are in any position to dispute.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Elder Dinichthys
msgctxt "Item:29743:0:2"
msgid "elder dinichthys"
msgstr "старые динихтисы"

#. ja: メルトール海峡の生態系上位に位置する大型甲冑魚<br>[魚拓額縁G3に設定可能]
#. de: Dieser große Panzerfisch steht in der Straße von Merlthor am oberen Ende der Nahrungskette. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe L ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Un poisson fossile géant qui domine la chaîne alimentaire du détroit de Merlthor.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de grande taille]
#. column 0: elder dinichthys
#. column 2: elder dinichthys
#. column 9: Elder Dinichthys
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:29743:0:8"
msgid "Swims about the Strait of Merlthor as though it owns the place─a claim which few of the other inhabitants are in any position to dispute.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]"
msgstr "Плавает по Мелторскому проливу так, будто здесь всё принадлежит ему. Да и мало кто из местных обитателей способен с этим поспорить.<br><br>[Можно выставить в рамке для крупного ихтиопринта.]"

#. ja: エルダー・ディニクティス
#. de: Tiefsee-Dunkleosteus
#. fr: Dinichthys ancien
#. column 0: elder dinichthys
#. column 2: elder dinichthys
#. column 8: Swims about the Strait of Merlthor as though it owns the place─a claim which few of the other inhabitants are in any position to dispute.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:29743:0:9"
msgid "Elder Dinichthys"
msgstr "Старый динихтис"

#. ja: ドランカードフィッシュ
#. de: Trunkenbold
#. fr: psychrolutes aviné
#. column 2: drunkfish
#. column 8: If you had a face like this, you'd look sad, too.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
#. column 9: Drunkfish
msgctxt "Item:29744:0:0"
msgid "drunkfish"
msgstr "рыба-пьяница"

#. de: Trunkenbolde
#. fr: psychrolutes avinés
#. column 0: drunkfish
#. column 8: If you had a face like this, you'd look sad, too.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
#. column 9: Drunkfish
msgctxt "Item:29744:0:2"
msgid "drunkfish"
msgstr "рыбы-пьяницы"

#. ja: 海底に棲息する稀少な深海魚<br>ガラディオン湾沖合の稀少魚<br>[魚拓額縁G2に設定可能]
#. de: Der Trunkenbold lebt vorwiegend am Meeresgrund und ist ein seltener Fisch aus den tiefen Gewässern der Galadion-Bucht. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe M ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Un poisson des abysses à l'allure étrange.<br>Rarissime, on l'aperçoit parfois dans la baie de Galadion.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de taille moyenne]
#. column 0: drunkfish
#. column 2: drunkfish
#. column 9: Drunkfish
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:29744:0:8"
msgid "If you had a face like this, you'd look sad, too.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]"
msgstr "С таким лицом и правда немудрено выглядеть печально.<br><br>[Можно выставить в рамке для среднего ихтиопринта.]"

#. ja: ドランカードフィッシュ
#. de: Trunkenbold
#. fr: Psychrolutes aviné
#. column 0: drunkfish
#. column 2: drunkfish
#. column 8: If you had a face like this, you'd look sad, too.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:29744:0:9"
msgid "Drunkfish"
msgstr "Рыба-пьяница"

#. ja: リトルリヴァイアサン
#. de: klein[a] Leviathan
#. fr: mini-Léviathan
#. column 2: little Leviathans
#. column 8: Even a greatly scaled-down (pun very much intended) version of the Lord of the Whorl is more than a match for all but the most experienced fishers.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Little Leviathan
msgctxt "Item:29745:0:0"
msgid "little Leviathan"
msgstr "маленький Левиафан"

#. de: klein[a] Leviathane
#. fr: mini-Léviathan
#. column 0: little Leviathan
#. column 8: Even a greatly scaled-down (pun very much intended) version of the Lord of the Whorl is more than a match for all but the most experienced fishers.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Little Leviathan
msgctxt "Item:29745:0:2"
msgid "little Leviathans"
msgstr "маленькие Левиафаны"

#. ja: 帯のような長い魚体を持つ獰猛な深海魚<br>メルトール海峡南の稀少魚<br>[魚拓額縁G3に設定可能]
#. de: Der kleine Leviathan ist ein Tiefseefisch mit langem elegant geschwungenem Körper. Er gilt als angriffslustiger Fisch und kommt in der südlichen Straße von Merlthor vor. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe L ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Cette espèce nouvellement découverte ressemble au Primordial dont elle tire son nom.<br>Rarissime, on l'aperçoit parfois au sud du détroit de Merlthor.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de grande taille]
#. column 0: little Leviathan
#. column 2: little Leviathans
#. column 9: Little Leviathan
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:29745:0:8"
msgid "Even a greatly scaled-down (pun very much intended) version of the Lord of the Whorl is more than a match for all but the most experienced fishers.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]"
msgstr "Даже сильно уменьшенная версия Владыки Вихря творения — каламбур вполне намеренный — даст фору кому угодно, кроме самых опытных рыбаков.<br><br>[Можно выставить в рамке для крупного ихтиопринта.]"

#. ja: リトルリヴァイアサン
#. de: Kleiner Leviathan
#. fr: Mini-Léviathan
#. column 0: little Leviathan
#. column 2: little Leviathans
#. column 8: Even a greatly scaled-down (pun very much intended) version of the Lord of the Whorl is more than a match for all but the most experienced fishers.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:29745:0:9"
msgid "Little Leviathan"
msgstr "Маленький Левиафан"

#. ja: シーサバトン
#. de: Eisenfuß
#. fr: sabaton des mers
#. column 2: sabatons
#. column 8: Strangely for a mollusk, its body is covered in hard scales in addition to the more common shell. Many predators will steer clear of them simply because they are a bother to eat.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
#. column 9: Sabaton
msgctxt "Item:29746:0:0"
msgid "sabaton"
msgstr "морской сабатон"

#. de: Eisenfüße
#. fr: sabatons des mers
#. column 0: sabaton
#. column 8: Strangely for a mollusk, its body is covered in hard scales in addition to the more common shell. Many predators will steer clear of them simply because they are a bother to eat.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
#. column 9: Sabaton
msgctxt "Item:29746:0:2"
msgid "sabatons"
msgstr "морские сабатоны"

#. ja: 頑強な金属のウロコを形成した稀少な巻貝<br>ロータノ海沖合の稀少魚<br>[魚拓額縁G2に設定可能]
#. de: Eine seltene Meeresschnecke, deren Haus aus besonders harten Schuppen besteht und die in der Rhotano-See heimisch ist. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe M ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Un étrange mollusque dont la coquille est recouverte d'écailles aussi dures que l'acier.<br>Rarissime, on l'aperçoit parfois dans la mer de Rhotano.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de taille moyenne]
#. column 0: sabaton
#. column 2: sabatons
#. column 9: Sabaton
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:29746:0:8"
msgid "Strangely for a mollusk, its body is covered in hard scales in addition to the more common shell. Many predators will steer clear of them simply because they are a bother to eat.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]"
msgstr "Для моллюска он необычен: помимо раковины, его тело покрыто твёрдой чешуёй. Хищники часто обходят его стороной — слишком уж хлопотно есть такую добычу.<br><br>[Можно выставить в рамке для среднего ихтиопринта.]"

#. ja: シーサバトン
#. de: Eisenfuß
#. fr: Sabaton des mers
#. column 0: sabaton
#. column 2: sabatons
#. column 8: Strangely for a mollusk, its body is covered in hard scales in addition to the more common shell. Many predators will steer clear of them simply because they are a bother to eat.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:29746:0:9"
msgid "Sabaton"
msgstr "Морской сабатон"

#. ja: 海の流星
#. de: Meerschnuppe
#. fr: étoile filante des mers
#. column 2: shooting stars
#. column 8: One's chances of seeing an actual shooting star are greater than that of being able to observe one of these rare wavekin in its natural habitat.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]
#. column 9: Shooting Star
msgctxt "Item:29747:0:0"
msgid "shooting star"
msgstr "морская падающая звезда"

#. de: Meerschnuppen
#. fr: étoiles filantes des mers
#. column 0: shooting star
#. column 8: One's chances of seeing an actual shooting star are greater than that of being able to observe one of these rare wavekin in its natural habitat.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]
#. column 9: Shooting Star
msgctxt "Item:29747:0:2"
msgid "shooting stars"
msgstr "морские падающие звёзды"

#. ja: サハギン族が珍重する紅色の海水魚<br>メルトール海峡北の稀少魚<br>[魚拓額縁G1に設定可能]
#. de: Ein seltener Salz<shy>was<shy>ser<shy>fisch, den die Sahagin verehren. Heimisch in der nördlichen Straße von Merlthor. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe S ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Un poisson marin aux écailles rouge vif, considéré comme précieux par les Sahuagins.<br>Rarissime, on l'aperçoit parfois dans le détroit nord de Merlthor.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de petite taille]
#. column 0: shooting star
#. column 2: shooting stars
#. column 9: Shooting Star
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:29747:0:8"
msgid "One's chances of seeing an actual shooting star are greater than that of being able to observe one of these rare wavekin in its natural habitat.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]"
msgstr "Увидеть настоящую падающую звезду куда проще, чем заметить в естественной среде обитания эту редкую рыбу.<br><br>[Можно выставить в рамке для мелкого ихтиопринта.]"

#. ja: 海の流星
#. de: Meerschnuppe
#. fr: Étoile filante des mers
#. column 0: shooting star
#. column 2: shooting stars
#. column 8: One's chances of seeing an actual shooting star are greater than that of being able to observe one of these rare wavekin in its natural habitat.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:29747:0:9"
msgid "Shooting Star"
msgstr "Морская падающая звезда"

#. ja: ハンマーロブスター
#. de: Hammer-Hummer
#. fr: marteaupince
#. column 2: hammerclaws
#. column 8: While most wavekin object quite strongly to being caught on a hook, these crustaceans make life especially difficult for anglers in retaliation. If they are not pinching fingers, they are flailing wildly with their heavy claws, both of which most fishers should and do go to great lengths to avoid.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
#. column 9: Hammerclaw
msgctxt "Item:29748:0:0"
msgid "hammerclaw"
msgstr "молотокраб"

#. de: Hammer-Hummer
#. fr: marteaupinces
#. column 0: hammerclaw
#. column 8: While most wavekin object quite strongly to being caught on a hook, these crustaceans make life especially difficult for anglers in retaliation. If they are not pinching fingers, they are flailing wildly with their heavy claws, both of which most fishers should and do go to great lengths to avoid.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
#. column 9: Hammerclaw
msgctxt "Item:29748:0:2"
msgid "hammerclaws"
msgstr "молотокрабы"

#. ja: 大型の鋏をハンマーに喩えられる肉食のロブスター<br>メルトール海峡北の稀少魚<br>[魚拓額縁G2に設定可能]
#. de: Eine große, aber seltene Hummerart, deren Fleisch als äußerst köstlich gilt. Lebt in der nördlichen Straße von Merlthor. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe M ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Un homard carnivore dont les énormes pinces ressemblent à des marteaux.<br>Rarissime, on l'aperçoit parfois dans le détroit nord de Merlthor.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de taille moyenne]
#. column 0: hammerclaw
#. column 2: hammerclaws
#. column 9: Hammerclaw
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:29748:0:8"
msgid "While most wavekin object quite strongly to being caught on a hook, these crustaceans make life especially difficult for anglers in retaliation. If they are not pinching fingers, they are flailing wildly with their heavy claws, both of which most fishers should and do go to great lengths to avoid.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]"
msgstr "Большинство рыб отчаянно сопротивляется, когда попадается на крючок, но эти ракообразные превращают рыбалку в настоящее мучение. То пальцы клешнями щиплют, то размахивают тяжёлыми клешнями изо всех сил. Рыбаки стараются держаться от них подальше — и правильно делают.<br><br>[Можно выставить в рамке для среднего ихтиопринта.]"

#. ja: ハンマーロブスター
#. de: Hammer-Hummer
#. fr: Marteaupince
#. column 0: hammerclaw
#. column 2: hammerclaws
#. column 8: While most wavekin object quite strongly to being caught on a hook, these crustaceans make life especially difficult for anglers in retaliation. If they are not pinching fingers, they are flailing wildly with their heavy claws, both of which most fishers should and do go to great lengths to avoid.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:29748:0:9"
msgid "Hammerclaw"
msgstr "Молотокраб"

#. ja: キー・オブ・ヘヴン
#. de: Himmelspforte
#. fr: clef du paradis
#. column 2: heavenskeys
#. column 8: Due to being highly poisonous, it is believed to send those who eat of its flesh to the heavens. Compared to the seven hells, this may prove a more desirable destination.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]
#. column 9: Heavenskey
msgctxt "Item:29749:0:0"
msgid "heavenskey"
msgstr "ключ от рая"

#. de: Himmelspforten
#. fr: clefs du paradis
#. column 0: heavenskey
#. column 8: Due to being highly poisonous, it is believed to send those who eat of its flesh to the heavens. Compared to the seven hells, this may prove a more desirable destination.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]
#. column 9: Heavenskey
msgctxt "Item:29749:0:2"
msgid "heavenskeys"
msgstr "ключи от рая"

#. ja: 幻海流のなか現れる大型のヘヴンリーフィッシュ<br>ガラディオン湾沖合の稀少魚<br>[魚拓額縁G1に設定可能]
#. de: Ein besonders großer Himmelsfisch, der vor allem in Phantomströmungen vorkommt. Gilt als selten und lebt in den tiefen Gewässern der Galadion-Bucht. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe S ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Un poisson-papillon élyséen géant vivant dans les courants spectraux.<br>Rarissime, on l'aperçoit parfois au large de la baie de Galadion.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de petite taille]
#. column 0: heavenskey
#. column 2: heavenskeys
#. column 9: Heavenskey
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:29749:0:8"
msgid "Due to being highly poisonous, it is believed to send those who eat of its flesh to the heavens. Compared to the seven hells, this may prove a more desirable destination.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]"
msgstr "Считается, что тот, кто попробует эту чрезвычайно ядовитую рыбу, отправится прямиком на небеса. Уж лучше, чем в семь преисподних.<br><br>[Можно выставить в рамке для мелкого ихтиопринта.]"

#. ja: キー・オブ・ヘヴン
#. de: Himmelspforte
#. fr: Clef du paradis
#. column 0: heavenskey
#. column 2: heavenskeys
#. column 8: Due to being highly poisonous, it is believed to send those who eat of its flesh to the heavens. Compared to the seven hells, this may prove a more desirable destination.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:29749:0:9"
msgid "Heavenskey"
msgstr "Ключ от рая"

#. ja: ゴーストシャーク
#. de: Geisterhai
#. fr: requin-fantôme
#. column 2: ghost sharks
#. column 8: According to certain sources, it is able to appear spontaneously from any body of water. Such stories, however, are probably best ignored.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Ghost Shark
msgctxt "Item:29750:0:0"
msgid "ghost shark"
msgstr "акула-призрак"

#. de: Geisterhaie
#. fr: requins-fantômes
#. column 0: ghost shark
#. column 8: According to certain sources, it is able to appear spontaneously from any body of water. Such stories, however, are probably best ignored.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Ghost Shark
msgctxt "Item:29750:0:2"
msgid "ghost sharks"
msgstr "акулы-призраки"

#. ja: 幻海流のなか現れる大型のターニッシュシャーク<br>ガラディオン湾沖合の稀少魚<br>[魚拓額縁G3に設定可能]
#. de: Eine seltene Matthai-Art aus der Galadion-Bucht, die vor allem in Phantomströmungen vorkommt. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe L ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Un requin terni géant vivant dans les courants spectraux.<br>Rarissime, on l'aperçoit parfois au large de la baie de Galadion.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de grande taille]
#. column 0: ghost shark
#. column 2: ghost sharks
#. column 9: Ghost Shark
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:29750:0:8"
msgid "According to certain sources, it is able to appear spontaneously from any body of water. Such stories, however, are probably best ignored.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]"
msgstr "Говорят, она может внезапно появиться из любого водоёма. Но подобные истории лучше оставить без внимания.<br><br>[Можно выставить в рамке для крупного ихтиопринта.]"

#. ja: ゴーストシャーク
#. de: Geisterhai
#. fr: Requin-fantôme
#. column 0: ghost shark
#. column 2: ghost sharks
#. column 8: According to certain sources, it is able to appear spontaneously from any body of water. Such stories, however, are probably best ignored.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:29750:0:9"
msgid "Ghost Shark"
msgstr "Акула-призрак"

#. ja: クイックシルバーブレード
#. de: Quecksilberklinge
#. fr: lame vif-argent
#. column 2: quicksilver blades
#. column 8: While there may be larger and deadlier wavekin roaming the oceans, few can claim to be as hideous as this aberration of nature.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Quicksilver Blade
msgctxt "Item:29751:0:0"
msgid "quicksilver blade"
msgstr "ртутный клинок"

#. de: Quecksilberklingen
#. fr: lames vif-argent
#. column 0: quicksilver blade
#. column 8: While there may be larger and deadlier wavekin roaming the oceans, few can claim to be as hideous as this aberration of nature.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Quicksilver Blade
msgctxt "Item:29751:0:2"
msgid "quicksilver blades"
msgstr "ртутные клинки"

#. ja: 水銀の刃と呼ばれる獰猛な鮫<br>ガラディオン湾沖合の稀少魚<br>[魚拓額縁G3に設定可能]
#. de: Die seltenen Quecksilberklingen kommen in der Galadion-Bucht vor und gelten als eine besonders angriffslustige Haiart. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe L ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Un requin aussi redoutable qu'insaisissable.<br>Rarissime, on l'aperçoit parfois au large de la baie de Galadion.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de grande taille]
#. column 0: quicksilver blade
#. column 2: quicksilver blades
#. column 9: Quicksilver Blade
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:29751:0:8"
msgid "While there may be larger and deadlier wavekin roaming the oceans, few can claim to be as hideous as this aberration of nature.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]"
msgstr "В океанах водятся рыбы покрупнее и поопаснее, но мало кто из них может сравниться в отвратительном виде с этим порождением природы.<br><br>[Можно выставить в рамке для крупного ихтиопринта.]"

#. ja: クイックシルバーブレード
#. de: Quecksilberklinge
#. fr: Lame vif-argent
#. column 0: quicksilver blade
#. column 2: quicksilver blades
#. column 8: While there may be larger and deadlier wavekin roaming the oceans, few can claim to be as hideous as this aberration of nature.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:29751:0:9"
msgid "Quicksilver Blade"
msgstr "Ртутный клинок"

#. ja: リムレーンプリント
#. de: Llymlaens Mal[p]
#. fr: empreinte de Llymlaen
#. column 2: Navigator's prints
#. column 8: This denizen of the deep can proudly claim to take its name from a goddess, even if the tale behind it does involve being stepped on by said goddess.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
#. column 9: Navigator's Print
msgctxt "Item:29752:0:0"
msgid "Navigator's print"
msgstr "отпечаток Мореплавательницы"

